# 8. Geographic information in the supplied file

The supplied sample already contains latitude and longitude for:

```text
96 / 105 places
```

Therefore most map functionality can work without external geocoding.

Nine locations currently have no coordinates.

These must remain valid place records.

A place without coordinates must be represented as:

```text
known place
geographic position unresolved
```

It must not be treated as an unknown place.

The initial version must not automatically send these unresolved place names to an online geocoder.

