# 54. Client-side routing on GitHub Pages

GitHub Pages does not provide an application server to rewrite arbitrary URLs back to the React entry point.

Therefore either:

1. use hash-based client-side routing; or
2. avoid URL-based routing and keep application navigation in React state.

Do not create a deployment that works from the homepage but produces 404 errors when views are opened directly.

For this application, URL routing is not a core requirement.

A simple single-page interface with local view state is preferred.

