# 57. Codex implementation rules

Codex must follow these constraints:

1. Do not add a backend.
2. Do not add Vercel.
3. Do not add authentication.
4. Do not add an online database.
5. Do not transmit genealogy data externally.
6. Do not add automatic online geocoding.
7. Do not commit the supplied genealogy CSV.
8. Do not treat the CSV as one flat table.
9. Preserve original imported values.
10. Keep import logic separate from the canonical model.
11. Model families independently from people.
12. Support multiple children per family.
13. Support missing parents.
14. Distinguish ancestor slots from unique people.
15. Preserve date precision.
16. Prefer vector genealogy exports.
17. Write tests for genealogy calculations.
18. Do not silently change requirements.
19. Document assumptions where source semantics are ambiguous.
20. Do not add unrelated genealogy functionality simply because competing genealogy applications contain it.

